<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Odo the Great</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 735</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a> · Also known as Odo of Aquitaine, Eudes of Aquitaine</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Odo the Great was Duke of Aquitaine from about 700 to 735, ruling a virtually independent realm south of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/loire">Loire</a>. In 721 he defeated an Umayyad army besieging <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toulouse">Toulouse</a>, one of the first checks on the Muslim advance into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaul">Gaul</a>. Routed by Abd al-Rahman near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bordeaux">Bordeaux</a> in 732, he sought help from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-martel">Charles Martel</a> and fought beside him at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-tours">Battle of Tours</a>.</p></div>
